239. Sliding Window Maximum

This problem is a classic example where we can move from Brute Force → Better → Optimal Monotonic Deque.

Problem

Given an integer array nums and an integer k, find the maximum element in every contiguous window of size k.

Example:

nums = [1,3,-1,-3,5,3,6,7]
k = 3


Windows:
[1, 3, -1]  → 3
[3, -1, -3] → 3
[-1,-3, 5]  → 5
[-3, 5, 3]  → 5
[5, 3, 6]   → 6
[3, 6, 7]   → 7


Answer = [3,3,5,5,6,7]

Approach 1: Brute Force
Idea

For every possible window:

Start at index i.
Look at the next k elements.
Find their maximum.
Store it.

For example:

nums = [1,3,-1,-3,5,3,6,7]
k = 3


i = 0 → [1,3,-1] → max = 3
i = 1 → [3,-1,-3] → max = 3
i = 2 → [-1,-3,5] → max = 5
...

Code
class Solution {
    public int[] maxSlidingWindow(int[] nums, int k) {
        int n = nums.length;


        int[] ans = new int[n - k + 1];
        int index = 0;


        for (int i = 0; i <= n - k; i++) {


            int max = Integer.MIN_VALUE;


            for (int j = i; j < i + k; j++) {
                max = Math.max(max, nums[j]);
            }


            ans[index++] = max;
        }


        return ans;
    }
}

